  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a4da58d2dc2409c459ef20449bf92a90, type: 3}
  m_Name: Truss
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  lessonId: LESSON004
  lessonTitle: What is Truss
  lessonImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: c7ad14becd77b714a820300c6ed3a180, type: 3}
  popupDescription: A truss bridge uses <b><#E09500>interconnected structural members
    arranged mainly in triangles</color></b> to efficiently support and distribute
    loads.
  almanacImage: {fileID: 0}
  lessonDescription: 'A truss bridge uses a framework of straight structural members
    connected to form stable arrangements, most notably <b><#E09500>triangular units</color></b>.
    When loads act on the bridge, forces are carried through the interconnected members,
    with individual members primarily resisting <b><#E09500>tension or compression</color></b>.
    The triangular configuration provides structural rigidity and allows substantial
    loads to be carried efficiently. '
